{
  "_doc": "CLI client conformance (SPEC §7G.10, §7G.11) over conformance/media/fake-cli/fake-cli.sh — see fake-cli/README.md for the exact harness steps. client = grok|codex. Placeholders: {out} the fake's out dir, {dir} gather.dir, {cwd} in expectArgv = must equal <out>/cwd.txt byte for byte after removing its one trailing newline (the fake writes `pwd -P`; D17: the client passes the realpath of its temp dir, so no symlink resolution on either side). command (when present) replaces the fake command entirely (spawn-failure case). env is set in the TEST process (the child inherits it; Codex's folder lookup reads it). expectExists / expectMissing: paths that must / must not exist after the run. expectNoSpawn: argv.txt must not exist. maxElapsedMs: the call must return within it (kill on timeout). Other fields as in clients.json. modelParts (SPEC §7G.6 model visibility): the parts of this tool result that message assembly (§8A) emits to the model — only image parts; video/audio parts stay in RunResult.files and toolCalls[].parts only. Assert with the port's assembly function on a transcript containing this tool result. ctxTimeoutMs (D12): function face only, ctx.deadline = now + ctxTimeoutMs; errorPrefix asserts the message start. D9 (SPEC §7G.12): when modelParts is [] the tool-result content the port sends to the model is the plain output string in every message style incl. Anthropic — never an empty content array, never a placeholder; assert it with the same assembly function. D19: a CLI client that does not accept a canonical arg is skipped (never spawned) ⇒ the joined 'media: no client available for …' error. D20 runFilePath / D21 noUsage: as in clients.json. D21: Grok's end-event costUsdTicks ⇒ usage.raw.costUsdTicks, never converted; total_cost_usd is ignored.",
